experiment: exsweep
  SHORT RUN — 100000 ticks against a minimum of 6800000.   reward buys the between-word SEPARATION and the lesson buys the
  ASSIGNMENT -- a double dissociation at 10.6 and 6.7 SE. So does phasic
  variability control help the assignment? `exploration.sensitivity` is
  the only reward-driven knob aimed at `vocal` and nothing else
  (`explore_scale` 1.0 there, 0.0 on all six others) and it ships at 0.0.
  A four-rung ladder 0/10/30/100, every arm TAUGHT. The window was derived
  off `babble`'s existing exploration print rather than guessed:
  |reward_fast - reward_slow| peaks at 0.001-0.003, so s~250 hits the 0.35
  floor and 600 clips, which is why the 500 in the genome comment left
  five of nine creatures too quiet to score. kRead because
  `dna/default.toml` has no kContext module, so on the genome the gate
  runs this on, the criterion is unreachable -- every verdict is PRINTED
  Everything below is printed for debugging and is NOT a
  measurement; this run cannot pass whatever it reads.

  instrument        exsweep   trial seed 000000000135c269   35 a ladder on exploration.sensitivity, every arm TAUGHT
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  the question      reward buys the separation and the lesson buys the
                    assignment. Does phasic variability control help the
                    assignment? `sensitivity` is the only reward-driven
                    knob aimed at vocal and nothing else, and it ships OFF.
  the ladder        sensitivity 0 / 10 / 30 / 100. The pre-flight
                    derived the scale off `babble`: |reward_fast -
                    reward_slow| peaks at 0.001-0.003, so s ~ 250 hits the
                    0.35 floor and 600 clips. Usable window is [10, 100].
  the primary       paired `direction - its own null`, s 100 against s 0,
                    plus the dose-response across all four rungs.
  PRE-REGISTERED    (a) direction MOVES with s; sign NOT predicted, since
                        phasic control could help the rotation or fight it.
                    (b) `within`'s MEAN DOES NOT move, because the
                        pre-flight read e_mean at 0.997-1.000 for every s.
                        A material fall refutes that reading of the knob.
  the manipulation  scored utterances must FALL monotonically with s --
                    `babble` lost 25% of its vocalisations at s = 100. An
                    IDENTICAL count across arms means the genome edit did
                    not land, which is how the pre-flight's first sweep
                    measured one creature six times.

